<p>Hey again, thanks for clarifying things for me!<br />
Anyway, on with the crit:</p>
<p>So at the moment this concept seems like a giant, many-tentacled middle finger to the whole oceanic ecosystem. This isn't inherently bad, but my main problem is that the narrative doesn't really go anywhere. People die, people go insane by looking at it, and that's the end. There isn't any twist, some subversion, a big reveal, anything. I'd suggest working on your narrative a bit more (sorry to be vague) and adding a twist or something.<br />
I also wouldn't recommend tying it into SCP-3069. While they both have detrimental effects on the ocean, that is where their similarities end.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Narrative&nbsp;Suggestions&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Might&nbsp;be&nbsp;worth&nbsp;a&nbsp;try?&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>What if these leviathans were actually responsible for maintaining life-harbouring levels of salt, and now they're waking up (presumably, they're mega pissed that we're polluting the ocean)?</p>
<p>What if a sample of their DNA reveals it is the exact same as a common species of eel, leaving researchers frantic to find what caused the eel to change into this?</p>
<p>This is all I could think of for now, hopefully it provides some inspiration!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, that's it for my recrit, hope this helps!</p>

