<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">[Holdplacer]</span></p>
<p>So, this really reminds me of a much weaker version of SCP-3000. Given that we know the captain is the last survivor of the event following the SCP's discovery, we can kind of surmise that anything anyone attempts to do in the logs will ultimately end in failure. This is not necessarily a bad thing though, as you can make the other bodies the Foundation found anomalous or interesting in and of themselves, like in the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1936">Daleport</a> SCP.</p>
<p>I don't really understand how any of its anomalous abilities relate to one another thematically. It's an antimemetic thing, but why can it change the salinity of water? Why's it got seven pupils? And how and why would the Captain cut a deal with this thing in the first place? These are narrative loose ends that should be tied up, as they can leave readers confused and wondering about the wrong thing.</p>

