<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I haven't read through all the other critiques. Forgive me if this is redundant.</p>
<p>Seems like three distinct stories:</p>
<ol>
<li>The article describing the entity itself and its containment procedures</li>
<li>The story of the the relationship of the sea captain with this creature and (and its capture?)</li>
<li>The story of a Foundation screw-up that creates a potential extinction-level event</li>
</ol>
<p>There's a lot there and it sounds difficult to pull off. Have you considered focusing on just one of these stories?</p>
<p>Lastly, I can't tell if the potential extinction-level event is caused by containing the entity. Is the solution simply to return it to the sea? If it's not actively destroying seagoing vessels since the Spanish Armada, maybe it's better tracked in place.</p>
<p>p.s. I do not have green light privileges.</p>
</div>
